Description: standalone local file search service for Bianbu devices
 Bibit filesearch indexes local documents (txt/md/docx/pdf/xlsx/pptx/code/png/jpg)
 and provides semantic search over them: embedding + BM25 hybrid retrieval,
 NL query parsing into deterministic filters (time range / directories /
 file types), and a unified {code, message, data} REST API. It is installed
 under /opt/bibit-filesearch.
 .
 OCR runs PP-OCR, PaddleOCR's detection/classification/recognition models,
 through onnxruntime. Its orientation classifier reads sideways and
 upside-down text directly, so no rotation preprocessing is needed, and
 inference is offloaded to the SpaceMIT NPU by a small resident C++ helper
 (SpaceMITExecutionProvider via /opt/bibit-filesearch/ocr-ep/ep_worker). That
 helper links libspacemit_ep.so and libonnxruntime.so, both shipped by
 spacemit-onnxruntime; without it OCR still works on CPU, only slower
 (measured 1.7-2.9x on real images, mean 2.26x, identical text). There is no
 second OCR engine: a failed recognition is reported as a failed file with a
 reason instead of being silently read by a worse engine.
